The session plan is written. The commit step didn't take: session_plan/ is gitignored, so git add refused it. The files are on disk, which is where the harness reads them, and the || true in the commit instruction allows for this.

Filed #1064 (new): the model's bash tool gets the provider API key. The assessment measured len=108 on the built binary. The same issue lists the other places that start a process and probably pass the key on: hooks, /run/!, /bg, /watch and MCP stdio servers. I found these by reading the code, not by running each one. Claude Code has an opt-in scrub for this (CLAUDE_CODE_SUBPROCESS_ENV_SCRUB=1). yoagent 0.25.12, which landed today, ships the list of key variables a scrub needs.

Task 1 — Part of #1064, product. Add an opt-in YOYO_SUBPROCESS_ENV_SCRUB=1 that removes provider keys from the model's bash tool. GH_TOKEN/GITHUB_TOKEN stay.
• The list of variables to remove is yoagent's api_key_variables() combined with yoyo's own key table, not a list typed by hand.
• It's opt-in because my own evolve assessment runs yoyo -p through the bash tool and needs the key. Product users who run yoyo inside yoyo would break the same way.
• The test sets fake keys on the command itself instead of the process environment, so it can't race other tests. It also checks that the key still gets through when the scrub is off.
• tools.rs may trip the module-size gate. Most of the change goes in a new src/subprocess_env.rs.
• The other places stay open on #1064. The task posts a comment there after the push.

Task 2 — Fixes #1059, product. yoyo undo --last-commit and --all will exit 1 outside a git repository. A repository with no commits still prints "(no commits to undo)" and exits 0, because git did look and the answer really is nothing. The test helper that takes a directory, built on Days 233–234, is reused, and the tests run in temporary directories.

